# Testing

- Name tests after behaviour (`Concurrent_buyers_cannot_oversell_the_last_units`, `'rolls back only the failed item'`).
  Assert outcomes users or callers can observe; avoid asserting implementation details or snapshots.
- Frontend unit tests: Vitest + TestBed, `provideHttpClientTesting` with `HttpTestingController`; zoneless — use
  `TestBed.tick()` / `fixture.whenStable()`. Test hosts must be `OnPush`. No non-null assertions; use helpers.
- State behaviour is tested once in `libs/state/contracts/src/testing/state-contract-suite.ts` and executed for both
  variants. Add NgRx-specific tests only for reducers/selectors.
- Backend unit tests (`Shop.Api.UnitTests`): pure domain/pricing logic, no database, no Docker.
- Backend integration tests (`Shop.Api.IntegrationTests`): `WebApplicationFactory` + real PostgreSQL (Testcontainers or
  `SHOP_TEST_CONNECTION_STRING` pointing at a database whose name contains `test`). Never mock EF Core.
- E2E (`apps/web-e2e`): arrange data through the API helpers (`support/api.ts`) with unique names; select by role/label
  first, `data-testid` second; every test must pass in both projects (`signals`, `ngrx`). Never add fixed sleeps.
- A failing test is information: fix the code or the test's wrong assumption, never weaken the assertion to go green.
